  <div class="ga-mandua-lead">
    <strong>Original High-Altitude Finger Millet (Mandua / Koda) Flour</strong> — slowly stone-ground in traditional Himalayan watermills (Gharats). 100% pure, chemical-free, and nutrient-dense mountain superfood.
  </div>

  <p style="font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #444;">
    Cultivated across high-elevation Himalayan terrace farms of Uttarakhand, <strong>Mandua (Finger Millet / Ragi)</strong> has been the nutritional backbone of Pahadi communities for centuries. Grown in unpolluted mountain air and fed by pure glacial springs without synthetic pesticides, our grains are carefully cleaned and cold-milled in traditional stone mills. This cold stone-grinding process prevents friction heat, locking in natural dietary fibers, active enzymes, and vital minerals.
  </p>

