  <h3 class="ga-mandua-section-title">Pahadi Kitchen Culinary Guide</h3>
  <div class="ga-mandua-recipe-grid">
    <div class="ga-mandua-recipe-box">
      <span class="ga-mandua-recipe-badge">Traditional Staple</span>
      <h4 class="ga-mandua-recipe-h">Pahadi Mandue Ki Roti</h4>
      <p class="ga-mandua-recipe-txt">
        Knead with warm water to a pliable dough. Gently pat between palms or roll between parchment sheets. Cook on an iron tawa until crisp and golden brown. Serve hot generously topped with <strong>Ghar Aangan Pahadi A2 Badri Cow Ghee</strong> and authentic <strong>Pahadi Pisyu Loon</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ga-mandua-recipe-box">
      <span class="ga-mandua-recipe-badge">Daily Family Upgrade</span>
      <h4 class="ga-mandua-recipe-h">50:50 Multigrain Rotis</h4>
      <p class="ga-mandua-recipe-txt">
        Mix 50% Mandua Flour with 50% whole wheat flour for everyday family rotis. They roll effortlessly like regular rotis, remain remarkably soft for lunchboxes, and provide twice the natural fiber and calcium for your family.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ga-mandua-recipe-box">
      <span class="ga-mandua-recipe-badge">Quick Breakfast</span>
      <h4 class="ga-mandua-recipe-h">Crispy Savory Cheela / Dosa</h4>
      <p class="ga-mandua-recipe-txt">
        Whisk Mandua flour with water or light curd, finely chopped onions, green chilies, coriander, and a pinch of cumin and Himalayan salt. Pour onto a hot tawa and cook until crisp on both sides for an energizing high-fiber breakfast.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ga-mandua-recipe-box">
      <span class="ga-mandua-recipe-badge">Winter Comfort</span>
      <h4 class="ga-mandua-recipe-h">Nutritious Halwa &amp; Porridge</h4>
      <p class="ga-mandua-recipe-txt">
        Slowly roast Mandua flour in Pahadi A2 Ghee until nutty and aromatic. Add water and dissolved <strong>Ghar Aangan Pahadi Gud (Jaggery)</strong>, stir continuously until thick and velvety, and finish with crushed cardamom and nuts.
      </p>
    </div>
